      {
        "id": 128468,
        "name": "jffdougan",
        "username": "jffdougan",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jffdougan/{size}/1882_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-21T14:39:30.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I have to admit that I haven't seen enough of the nominees to make informed decisions. Having 2 small kids (ages 9 and just under 5) really cuts down how much I get to see.</p><p>The only best picture nominee I\"ve seen any of is Grand Budapest, and I only got to see about 1/2 - my wife started feeling sick that night, and we didn't get a chance to finish it before it was due back at the library. Imitation Game is on my list for eventually, but it's probably going to have to wait on the library.</p><p>In Animated Feature, I've seen HttYD2, my wife took the kids to see Big Hero 6 at the early end of Christmas Break while I still had to work. I've seen the fury that the Lego Movie didn't get nominated, but I can't compare it to the remainder of the nominees. Even had it been nominated, I'd likely pick HttYD2 over it.</p><p>I tend to like some of the \"techie\" awards - Costumes, Score, Special Effects. (I don't know enough about make-up outside prosthetics to have informed opinions in that category.) Based only on trailers, I pick Into the Woods for Costumes, with Grand Budapest as my runner-up. I haven't seen enough of any of this year's Score nominees to form an opinion. Special Effects is a tough call for me, but I think that I pick Days of Future Past (with the caveat that I haven't seen either Guardians of the Galaxy or the Planet of the Apes installment).</p>",
