        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/c6cbf5/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-27T12:13:40.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Heh, I just watched <em>The Imitation Game</em> again and I'm actually surprised that niether Mark Strong or matthew Goode are up for Best Supporting Actor. It's easy for their impact to get lost behind Cumberbatch's central performance, but both gave really strong performances. I was also reminded at how tragically poor Keira Kneightly is at anything other than mooning with her eyes. I mean, how is it possible for an English actress to fail to put on a convincing English accent?</p>",
